{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Justice, justice shall you pursue, etc.</b> This comes to warn: when there are in a city two men who are outstanding in wisdom, and two others who are also wise but do not belong to the caliber of the first, a person should not say: since two men are able to instruct and judge with justice, I shall not trouble the outstanding ones to bear the burden of appointment to the judiciary — or because appointing them requires effort, he will refrain and content himself with the lesser ones. Scripture therefore says ״צֶדֶק צֶדֶק״ — meaning: even though you have found judges who are worthy, you are obligated to seek out those who are more worthy than they."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:39.804732497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}